-- `l4 batch` runs a PRINTED copy of the module. Each group below has a
-- definition named like a name the compiler makes up for it. Printed from
-- what the clauses compile to, the made-up name met the drafter's as source
-- and changed the answer, with no diagnostic; printed as the clauses the
-- drafter wrote, it cannot. tests-cli/Main.hs gives the answers.

DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

-- the binding of the later clauses (probe b2)
`the result of clauses 2 to 3` MEANS 7

@export later
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE later Red   IS `the result of clauses 2 to 3`
DECIDE later Green IS 2
DECIDE later c     IS 3

-- the binding of the last clause (probe b4)
`the result of clause 3` MEANS 100

@export fee
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE fee Red   IS 1
DECIDE fee Green IS `the result of clause 3` + 1
DECIDE fee c     IS 3

-- an input of a group with no GIVEN (probe b5), read through an export
-- that has one
`input 1` MEANS Blue

DECIDE untyped Red   IS `input 1`
DECIDE untyped Green IS Red
DECIDE untyped Blue  IS Green

@export through
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A Colour
DECIDE through c IS untyped c
